        "id": "abd9233a"
      },
      "source": [
        "# ASE Tutorial: Opening and Inspecting the xyz file\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook walks through:\n",
        "1. Reading an extended XYZ file with ASE\n",
        "2. Exploring basic `Atoms` properties\n",
        "3. Understanding the `atoms.info` dictionary\n",
        "4. Checking the correct shape of every data array\n",
        "5. Iterating over all frames\n",
        "\n",
        "The file is **XYZ** format — each frame's comment line contains JSON-serialised arrays that ASE automatically parses into `atoms.info`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7675456a"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 1. Imports"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "8c34656e"
      },
      "source": [
        "import ase.io\n",
        "import numpy as np"
      ],
      "execution_count": 3,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "de8fa539"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 2. Reading the XYZ File\n",
        "\n",
        "Pass `\":\"` as the index to read **all** frames, or `\":10\"` for the first 10."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "daead7a1"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Read all frames — returns a list of Atoms objects\n",
        "db = ase.io.read(\"SINGLET_SOC_ALL.xyz\", \":\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Total frames loaded : {len(db)}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Work with the first frame for exploration\n",
        "atoms = db[0]\n",
        "print(f\"Type of each element: {type(atoms)}\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6dcd96d1"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 3. Basic Atoms Properties"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "66c17a76"
      },
      "source": [
        "print(\"Number of atoms    :\", len(atoms))\n",
        "print(\"Chemical symbols   :\", list(atoms.symbols))\n",
        "print(\"Positions shape    :\", atoms.positions.shape)   # (N_atoms, 3)"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "469bf0ab"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 4. Listing All `atoms.info` Keys\n",
        "\n",
        "`atoms.info` is a plain Python `dict`. Every key in the extXYZ comment line ends up here, with JSON arrays already parsed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "fbf5fba8"
      },
      "source": [
        "print(\"Keys in atoms.info:\")\n",
        "for k in atoms.info:\n",
        "    print(\" \", k)"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "b06c4f6a"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 5. Shape Reference\n",
        "\n",
        "The dataset contains **4 electronic states** and **N = 23 atoms**.  \n",
        "The number of unique state pairs is `4 × (4-1) / 2 = 6`.\n",
        "\n",
        "| Key | Expected shape | Meaning |\n",
        "|---|---|---|\n",
        "| `energy` | `(1, 4)` | 1 geometry × 4 state energies |\n",
        "| `forces` | `(23, 4, 3)` | atoms × states × xyz |\n",
        "| `couplings` | `(23, 6, 3)` | atoms × state pairs × xyz |\n",
        "| `smooth_nacs` | `(23, 6, 3)` | smoothed NACs, same layout |\n",
        "| `socs` | `(1, 240)` | flat SOC vector |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "da16673b"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 6. Inspecting Each Key"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "506f1e38"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 6.1 Energy — shape `(1, 4)`"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "90bb1799"
      },
      "source": [
        "energy = np.array(atoms.info['REF_energy'])\n",
        "print(\"energy shape :\", energy.shape)   # (1, 4)\n",
        "print(\"values       :\", energy)"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "f5d960f5"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 6.2 Forces — shape `(N_atoms, 4, 3)`"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "abff3973"
      },
      "source": [
        "forces = np.array(atoms.info['REF_forces'])\n",
        "print(\"forces shape :\", forces.shape)   # (23, 4, 3)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Re-order to (n_states, N_atoms, 3) if you prefer state-first indexing\n",
        "forces_sf = forces.transpose(1, 0, 2)\n",
        "print(\"state-first  :\", forces_sf.shape)"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4005cbfc"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 6.3 Couplings — shape `(N_atoms, 6, 3)`"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "864c36e6"
      },
      "source": [
        "couplings = np.array(atoms.info['REF_smooth_nacs']) # Can adjust nacs key here\n",
        "print(\"couplings shape :\", couplings.shape)   # (23, 6, 3)"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "e5fb260b"
      },
      "source": [
        "### 6.5 Spin–Orbit Couplings — shape `(1, 240)` with labels"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "f41e65cb"
      },
      "source": [
        "socs = np.array(atoms.info['REF_socs'])\n",
        "print(\"socs shape   :\", socs.shape)          # (1, 240)"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "1ce38a5d"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 7. Sanity-Check Script\n",
        "\n",
        "Run this to verify all shapes are correct for every frame in the dataset."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "df301516"
      },
      "source": [
        "N        = len(atoms)                            # 23\n",
        "n_states = 4\n",
        "n_pairs  = n_states * (n_states - 1) // 2       # 6\n",
        "\n",
        "expected_shapes = {\n",
        "    'REF_energy'      : (1, n_states),\n",
        "    'REF_forces'      : (N, n_states, 3),\n",
        "    'REF_couplings'   : (N, n_pairs,  3),\n",
        "    'REF_smooth_nacs' : (N, n_pairs,  3),\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Checking frame 0 (N_atoms={N}, n_states={n_states}, n_pairs={n_pairs})\\n\")\n",
        "all_ok = True\n",
        "for key, expected in expected_shapes.items():\n",
        "    actual = np.array(atoms.info[key]).shape\n",
        "    ok = actual == expected\n",
        "    status = \"✓\" if ok else f\"✗  got {actual}\"\n",
        "    print(f\"  {key:22s}  expected {str(expected):15s}  {status}\")\n",
        "    all_ok = all_ok and ok\n",
        "\n",
        "print()\n",
        "print(\"All shapes correct!\" if all_ok else \"Some shapes are wrong — check above.\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "b7d0aae1"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 8. Iterating Over All Frames"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0f5d7966"
      },
      "source": [
        "print(f\"{'Frame':>6}  {'Min energy (eV)':>18}  {'Max |force| (eV/Å)':>20}\")\n",
        "print(\"-\" * 50)\n",
        "\n",
        "for i, frame in enumerate(db):\n",
        "    e = np.array(frame.info['REF_energy'])\n",
        "    f = np.array(frame.info['REF_forces'])\n",
        "    print(f\"{i:>6}  {e.min():>18.6f}  {np.abs(f).max():>20.6f}\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
